    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 12-layer dielectric anti-reflection coating on silicon substrate with air incidence at 0 degrees, unpolarized light. Materials: alternating Ta2O5 (high-index) and SiO2 (low-index), starting with Ta2O5 adjacent to air, ending with SiO2 adjacent to silicon substrate. Wavelength bands: 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm, equal weighting. Initialize thicknesses using the round 2 candidate 3 median profile [278.37, 280.71, 225.29, 319.00, 272.38, 278.42, 236.68, 306.82, 314.54, 282.11, 84.20, 74.18] nm with ±3% Gaussian perturbation applied to each layer. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with step-size multiplier reduced by 25% compared to previous iteration. Thickness bounds: 20-400 nm per layer. Objective: maximize joint mean transmittance across both bands. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and final thicknesses_nm for all candidates. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 1260-1360 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: low average reflectance in 1260-1360 nm band; low average reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflection in the specified bands. manufacturing constraints: maximum 12 layers; individual layer thickness between 20 nm and 400 nm; materials restricted to Ta2O5 and SiO2.",
